<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mande peoples</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mande peoples are a family of ethnic groups of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> who speak Mande languages, among them the Malinke, Bambara, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soninke">Soninke</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wangara">Dyula</a> and Mende. Their heartland, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manding">Manden</a> on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, was the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a> in the 13th century. Mande traders, especially the Dyula, carried commerce and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> far into the forest zone.</p></div>
